{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0122 adopted `vector` — a digest of each ticket, embedded and cosine-ranked — as the only candidate beating the lexical tier at k=5 (semantic recall@5 0.876 vs 0.823). rebar runs against diverse providers, so this tier must not be reachable through one vendor only, and an install with none must still get surfacing.\n\n## Constraints\n\n**Portability comes from the lexical tier, not this one.** The index sibling [rebar:47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88] ships retrieval and the surfacing sibling [rebar:80a5-cbb1-ef06-4ba5] the advisory, with no provider, credentials or network. This tier is an opt-in ranking upgrade that degrades to lexical whenever a provider is absent or failing; it replaces the scoring function and adds the build. k stays at 5, ADR 0122's scope.\n\n**The build never runs on the create path.** `find_similar` calls `catch_up` inline (`similar/__init__.py:62`) and the create advisory calls `find_similar` (`_commands/recent_creates.py:196`), so whatever catch-up does runs inside a user's create. Lexical catch-up belongs there: one `stat` per directory. A digest-and-embed pass does not — one LLM call plus one embed per ticket, network-bound. So catch-up never digests, embeds, or calls the build; unvectored entries are left alone, bounding per-create work at the lexical catch-up's cost however much of the corpus lacks vectors. The build is a separate explicit `build_vectors(tracker)` in `embedding.py` that a caller invokes. Until every live entry carries a current-key vector, queries degrade — a fresh or invalidated corpus is degraded, never a slow create, and converges when that call returns. Exposing it as a command or sweep is out of scope here.\n\n**Vendor-neutrality uses a seam the runtime ships.** `pydantic-ai-slim` 1.107.9 already backs `llm/providers.py`. Its embeddings API (`infer_embedding_model`, `Embedder`, `EmbeddingModel`) dispatches a `provider:model` string in the shape `providers.py` already uses.\n\n**A missing optional backend is expected, not a defect.** `pydantic-ai-slim` reaches rebar through `[agents]`, not core `dependencies`, and its per-vendor backends carry optional groups that raise `ImportError` naming the group when absent. `[openai]` and `[bedrock]` sit in the `dev` extra (`pyproject.toml:315`, `:318`), so AC2 fails rather than skips; `cohere` is in neither, so `cohere:embed-v4.0` is AC11's case.\n\n**Both model choices are configuration, unset by default.** `[llm] embedding_model` and `[llm] similar_digest_model`, read from `REBAR_LLM_EMBEDDING_MODEL` and `REBAR_LLM_SIMILAR_DIGEST_MODEL`, follow the existing `model` key's provider-qualified-string convention. Neither ships an active default: with `embedding_model` unset the query is the lexical tier's. `bedrock:amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` (1,024 dimensions, cosine) and `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0` are ADR 0122's measured values, recommended rather than applied. Where the parent [rebar:4e89-30b9-1666-4e53] calls the Titan string \"the configured default\" it means that recommendation; this leaf governs the key's default, which is unset.\n\n**The edit set the two keys require.** `llm/config.py` declares the fields; `llm/config_readers.py` resolves them via `_llm_str`, so each inherits the CLI>env>file>default precedence every `[llm]` string key has. `docs/env-vars.md` is GENERATED by `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` and drift-tested, so it is regenerated here. `tests/golden/config_surface.json` is NOT touched: it inventories only `_config_schema._SECTIONS`, which has no `[llm]` section. The census records an `[llm]` key under its environment name, so each carries a `# mechanism-ok: env_var …` marker naming this ticket.\n\n**Cosine ranking requires full current-key coverage.** Embedding spaces are not comparable across models, so the index's validity key folds the embedding-model identity and the pinned digest-prompt commit in alongside the sibling's freshness key; changing either invalidates those entries. rebar cosine-ranks only when EVERY live entry carries a current-key vector, and otherwise degrades, never ranking across a partial corpus or two embedding spaces.\n\n**Degrade** means retrieval returns the lexical tier's whole-corpus results, the create advisory carries them, a diagnostic is emitted and create exits 0.\n\n**Digest step.** The 4-field prompt pinned at `f147e08242f`, input capped at 40,000 characters, per ADR 0122. Recovery: decode the reply as JSON, else YAML; if neither yields a top-level object, extract the first balanced object embedded in the text; then unwrap a single wrapper key such as `ticket_digest` before reading the 4 fields. A mapping so recovered whose 4 fields are all empty increments `empties` and degrades without retry. Only a reply from which no object carrying the field names can be recovered increments `digest_unparsed` and is retried once; a retry that succeeds counts as a success. A reply unrecoverable on BOTH attempts increments `digest_failed`: that ticket is left unvectored, the build logs it and proceeds, and coverage is then short of full, so queries degrade until a later build recovers it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A `provider:model` string resolves via `infer_embedding_model` and retrieval cosine-ranks the vectors. Test: `TestEmbeddingModel`, assert the ordering.\n- [ ] A string for two distinct providers resolves to each provider's model. Test: parameterize `bedrock:`/`openai:`, assert the class.\n- [ ] No vendor name appears in a conditional in the retrieval or digest path. Test: assert no `_PROVIDER_PREFIXES` literal outside a default or docstring.\n- [ ] The digest model resolves from a provider-qualified string. Test: configure a non-Bedrock string, assert the resolved model.\n- [ ] Changing `[llm] embedding_model` invalidates the affected vectors. Test: build, reconfigure, assert they re-embed.\n- [ ] Changing the pinned digest-prompt commit invalidates them likewise. Test: build, repin, assert they re-embed.\n- [ ] A query without full current-key coverage degrades. Test: fail the provider after N of M, assert the advisory is lexical.\n- [ ] An interrupted re-embed never ranks across two embedding spaces. Test: change the key, fail after a subset, assert lexical not mixed.\n- [ ] With `embedding_model` unset, retrieval degrades. Test: assert the advisory equals lexical.\n- [ ] Both keys are unset by default. Test: assert each is `None` with neither env nor file set.\n- [ ] An absent optional backend degrades, naming the missing group. Test: `cohere:embed-v4.0`, assert status/advisory/diagnostic.\n- [ ] A provider denial or timeout degrades. Test: parameterize both, assert status/advisory/diagnostic.\n- [ ] An all-empty digest mapping degrades. Test: assert status/advisory/diagnostic.\n- [ ] `empties` counts every all-empty recovery. Test: feed ADR 0122's three shapes, assert it is 3.\n- [ ] A build completes despite all-empty digests. Test: the run indexes the remaining tickets.\n- [ ] An unrecoverable reply is retried once. Test: prose then success, assert `digest_unparsed` is 1.\n- [ ] A retry that succeeds counts as a success. Test: the ticket indexes and `digest_failed` is 0.\n- [ ] Unrecoverable on both attempts increments `digest_failed`. Test: prose twice, assert it is 1.\n- [ ] That build still finishes and later queries degrade. Test: the others index, the advisory is lexical.\n- [ ] `catch_up` does no digest or embedding work. Test: create with a stub provider configured, assert it is never called.\n- [ ] Create-path cost is flat in the unvectored share. Test: provider calls are 0 with none, some and all unvectored.\n- [ ] rebar's declared dependencies are unchanged. Test: the dependency lists are untouched in the diff.\n- [ ] `docs/env-vars.md` is regenerated carrying both variables. Test: `gen_env_registry.py` leaves no diff, drift tests pass.\n- [ ] `check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0, each mechanism marker-admitted naming this ticket.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0. Test: run it.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793617473211727395,"uuid":"790464f6-0314-4ca7-8a5b-6e04f2c8e8d0"}